<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Jan-Aug trade gap rises to CZK 100.9 bln.</title>
<headline>Czech Jan-Aug trade gap rises to CZK 100.9 bln.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech trade balance for the first eight months in 1996 rose to 100.9 billion crowns from a revised deficit of 86.1 billion for the January-July period, the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The trade deficit for the January-August period in 1995 was 59.5 billion crowns.  </p>
